# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# x402 merchant configuration (testnet)
#
# The active corridor below is Base Sepolia USDC → Tempo (Moderato) pathUSD.
# You only NEED to set USE_STUB_FACILITATOR and — for real settlement — DEST_ADDRESS.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Settlement mode — the one value most users touch.
#   true  — local stub: full 402 → pay → 200 flow, no facilitator/gateway/funds (default)
#   false — settle through a real Atum x402 facilitator (needs a funded payer + DEST_ADDRESS below)
USE_STUB_FACILITATOR=true

# Your receiving address on the destination chain.
# Required only when USE_STUB_FACILITATOR=false.
DEST_ADDRESS=0xYourMerchantAddressHere


# ─── Corridor ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The SOURCE is the network + token the payer funds from; the DEST is what the
# merchant receives. The corridor's CONTRACT ADDRESSES (escrow, fulfillment proxy,
# reserver, releaser, and the verifier endpoint) are NOT set here — the merchant
# resolves them from the gateway's GET /v1/defaults at startup, so they can't drift.
# (Verified: /v1/defaults returns exactly those addresses.)
#
# Only the verified Base <-> Tempo testnet corridor is supported here (EVM only —
# this example signs with ethers + Permit2). Values are a CAIP-2 network id + the
# bare token address, from https://docs.atum.xyz/get-started/reference/supported-assets
#
# To reverse direction, comment the active block and uncomment the alternative.

# Base Sepolia · USDC  ->  Tempo Moderato · pathUSD   (active default)
SOURCE_NETWORK=eip155:84532
SOURCE_ASSET=0x036CbD53842c5426634e7929541eC2318f3dCF7e
DEST_NETWORK=eip155:42431
DEST_ASSET=0x20C0000000000000000000000000000000000000

# Alternative — Tempo Moderato · pathUSD  ->  Base Sepolia · USDC
# SOURCE_NETWORK=eip155:42431
# SOURCE_ASSET=0x20C0000000000000000000000000000000000000
# DEST_NETWORK=eip155:84532
# DEST_ASSET=0x036CbD53842c5426634e7929541eC2318f3dCF7e


# ─── Endpoints (Atum-hosted) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Same host, two different values. The merchant appends /verify and /settle to
# FACILITATOR_URL, so the /x402/v1 prefix is part of that value; it appends /defaults
# to GATEWAY_URL, so that one stays a bare host. Copy each exactly as written.
#
# Both default (in src/merchant.ts) to the testnet pair, so you don't need to set them
# for testnet. For mainnet — where authorized by Atum — uncomment the mainnet pair.

# testnet (the defaults)
# GATEWAY_URL=https://payment-gw.production-testnet.atum.xyz
# FACILITATOR_URL=https://payment-gw.production-testnet.atum.xyz/x402/v1

# mainnet
# GATEWAY_URL=https://payment-gw.production-mainnet.atum.xyz
# FACILITATOR_URL=https://payment-gw.production-mainnet.atum.xyz/x402/v1

# ─── Demo: watch a slow settlement resolve ───────────────────────────────────
# How many attempts at a purchase the STUB reports as still settling before it settles.
# Set it to see the payer's re-attempt collect the outcome — the path a real cross-chain
# settlement takes when it outruns the gateway's ~30s synchronous window. Stub only.
#   STUB_PENDING_ATTEMPTS=2

# Everything else (amount, markup, deadlines) has working testnet defaults in
# src/merchant.ts. See the README to override them.
